  "solution": {
    "text": "Blocks&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> both move due to friction. But less friction is available to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> as compared to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> because the normal reaction between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is less. Maximum friction between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> can be<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> Maximum acceleration of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> can be<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Further <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Or <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Or <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>"
